# kex: check-only
# A method is only in reach through the imports at its call, and only what
# their `only:` lets through (kexhq/kex#570). `Net.HTTP.Server.localAddress`
# is not imported here, so `running.localAddress` is undefined. It checked
# clean instead, because the import of `Net.HTTP` counted whole, and BEAM then
# called the TCP listener's `localAddress`: `function_clause` at run time. A
# spec file got the same from `Net.HTTP.WebSocket`'s own `using Net.HTTP`.
using Net.HTTP, only: [Router]

foul address(running: Net.HTTP.Server.Running) = running.localAddress

main do
  IO.printLine(Router.build)
end
